{
  "about": "What schema expansion and the specification compiler refuse, and admit, before any record is read: a window reference's expansion (WINDOW-1), an aggregate derive binding that is a window operation (LOOKUP-22), grammar findings binding keeps at their authored paths (FORMULA-1), integer literals and handlers outside int's range (VALUE-5), redundant Parquet field types (INPUT-6), verification declarations (CHECK-4) and a qualified aggregate grouped by no output key (LOOKUP-19). The window cases expand a schema whose `windows` declare complete definitions and whose columns' derivations take a `row_number` window, written inline or by name; an unused malformed definition is found in either mode, and only `strict` reports a surviving unknown reference. The specification `value` derives the int column VALUE from SRC, read from input.csv with the schema ID, int, and each case writes VALUE's derivation, type or verifications, its row templates or its input; `aggregate_derive` derives VALUE with an aggregate whose derive binding V reads SRC.ID, and each of its cases writes V's derivation. Each case compares the fields its Rust table compared, and an `among` case finds its record by cause among the others.",
  "documents": {
    "value": {
      "yamaa": "1.0",
      "type": "spec",
      "domain": "TEST",
      "input": {"SRC": {"path": "input.csv"}},
      "keys": ["ID"],
      "columns": [
        {"name": "ID", "type": "int", "derivation": {"value": "SRC.ID"}},
        {"name": "VALUE", "type": "int", "derivation": {"value": 1}}
      ],
      "output": {"path": "result.csv", "columns": ["ID", "VALUE"]}
    },
    "aggregate_derive": {
      "yamaa": "1.0",
      "type": "spec",
      "domain": "TEST",
      "input": {"SRC": {"path": "input.csv"}},
      "keys": ["ID"],
      "columns": [
        {"name": "ID", "type": "int", "derivation": {"value": "SRC.ID"}},
        {"name": "VALUE", "type": "int", "derivation": {"value": {"aggregate": {"derivations": {"V": {"type": "int", "derivation": {"value": "SRC.ID"}}}, "expr": "SUM(V)"}}}}
      ],
      "output": {"path": "result.csv", "columns": ["ID", "VALUE"]}
    }
  },
